      "A U.S. listed exchange traded fund tracking the high-flying South Korean stock market is sharply lower in pre-market action as a wobble in risk appetite batters memory stocks.",
      "South Korea's Kospi index, which has more than doubled this year as chipmakers Samsung and SK Hynix surged, dipped 1.8% on Thursday in Seoul.",
      "However, traders seem to be anticipating further losses as the iShares MSCI South Korea ETF is down nearly 7%."
